zlib gzseek64(): no signed overflow in the range checks when gzungetc() has left the position negative.

Defect. gzungetc() on a read handle whose output buffer is empty decrements x.pos (gzread.c:588 at 99623ef7;
gzread.c:612 for a further push), so a push before any read leaves x.pos = -1. gzseek64 with SEEK_CUR then
computes pos = x.pos + skip = -1 and evaluates its guard `offset > GZ_OFF_MAX - pos` (gzlib.c:395):
GZ_OFF_MAX + 1 overflows z_off64_t, a signed overflow, for any offset. With SEEK_SET and an offset near
GZ_OFF_MAX the later displacement `pos - state->x.pos` (and the raw lseek offset) overflows the same way.

Fix. The SEEK_CUR guard is evaluated only for a positive pos, and a target whose displacement from a negative
x.pos does not fit in z_off64_t is refused (-1) before either displacement is computed.

Upstream. madler/zlib pull request #1361, "Avoid gzseek overflow after initial pushback" (open on 2026-11-15),
head commit ce2248ee97501aff83203a68a37369fa6c988eda (two commits on 757f0527: 2da30ec3, then ce2248ee). This is
ONLY the pull request's gzlib.c hunk (gzseek64, +5/-1), not its test/example.c hunk: the zlib team's copy of
that hunk (06-zlib-gzseek64-pr1361.patch, md5 2a8c147b11d0988a08695f35de23903a) with its paths rebased from
ext-base/zlib-checksum_fuzzer/ to the tree root and its index line kept. Its hunk is byte for byte the pull
request's gzlib.c hunk (`gh api repos/madler/zlib/pulls/1361` as a diff, gzlib.c index c3b3efc27..04220039c),
and c3b3efc is gzlib.c's blob at aef's pin 99623ef7, where it applies with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0`.

Scope. This patch is applied to the build of targets/zlib-sysfail_fuzzer ONLY, by the pin key LIB_PATCHES
(tools/ossfuzz/recipes.sh aef_lib_patches, on the build's copy of the tree): no other zlib target, and not
ext/zlib-sysfail_fuzzer/src, changes. The default patch stack (patches/github.com/madler/zlib/99623ef7.../)
does not carry it. A release build (AEF_RELEASE=1) applies none of LIB_PATCHES: it is a library-defect fix,
and the public release ships the library without those.

Provenance. ZLIB-8 (2026-11-15): Jason's answer "No new report; patch it" for the system-call failure driver.
The driver reaches this bug with no failure schedule (targets/zlib-sysfail_fuzzer/known-ub-ungetc-seek.dsl,
found by the ZLIB-8 review): on an unpatched build the UBSan flavours trap in gzseek64 (status 132) where plain
returns -1 (tests/check_sys_schedule.sh S6).

Author of the fix: the pull request's author (GitHub cla7aye15I4nd). Carried unchanged by Claude Opus 5.5
(aef, 2026-11-15).

diff --git a/gzlib.c b/gzlib.c
index c3b3efc..0422003 100644
--- a/gzlib.c
+++ b/gzlib.c
@@ -392,12 +392,16 @@ z_off64_t ZEXPORT gzseek64(gzFile file, z_off64_t offset, int whence) {
     /* compute the absolute position */
     pos = whence == SEEK_SET ? 0 :
           state->x.pos + (state->past ? 0 : state->skip);
-    if (offset > GZ_OFF_MAX - pos)
+    if (pos > 0 && offset > GZ_OFF_MAX - pos)
         return -1;                          /* would overflow z_off64_t */
     if (offset < -pos)
         return -1;                          /* before start of file */
     pos += offset;
 
+    /* the displacement from a negative position must fit in z_off64_t */
+    if (state->x.pos < 0 && pos > GZ_OFF_MAX + state->x.pos)
+        return -1;
+
     /* if within raw area while reading, just go there */
     if (state->mode == GZ_READ && state->how == COPY) {
         ret = LSEEK(state->fd, pos - state->x.pos - (z_off64_t)state->x.have,
